# Brigit/Brigte [wiki-old-irish-grammar §ā-stems; strachan1909-oldirish-paradigms pp.6-8;
# pokorny1914-oldirish-grammar §§136-138]. iā-stem ⟨-e -i⟩ finals are unchanged (no rule).
# The ī-stem is selected by SHAPE (O-21): polysyllabic with a final nucleus ⟨ai⟩ (glide) or
# plain ⟨i⟩ -> SYNC + ⟨-ae⟩ / ⟨-e⟩ (§41: /e/ is written ⟨-ae⟩ after a broad consonant,
# ⟨-e⟩ after a slender one). Written as append-then-delete, since a rule cannot both
